## 3. Escalation / error handling

The `validate` step's `MissingOwnerFieldsException` is routed by an escalation YAML keyed on the fully-qualified exception name:

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.MissingOwnerFieldsException.yml`

```yaml
handle:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.MissingOwnerFieldsExceptionHandler
```

Handler:
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/MissingOwnerFieldsExceptionHandler.java`

```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation;

import java.util.List;

import net.officefloor.plugin.section.clazz.Parameter;
import net.officefloor.web.ObjectResponse;
import org.springframework.http.HttpStatus;
import org.springframework.http.ResponseEntity;

public class MissingOwnerFieldsExceptionHandler {

    /** Response body: {@code {"errors": ["city", ...]}}. */
    public record MissingFields(List<String> errors) {
    }

    public void handle(@Parameter MissingOwnerFieldsException ex,
            ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<MissingFields>> response) {
        response.send(ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST)
                .body(new MissingFields(ex.getFields())));
    }
}
```

Exception:
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/MissingOwnerFieldsException.java`

```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation;

import java.util.List;

/**
 * Thrown when a create-owner request omits or blanks a required field. Handled by
 * {@link MissingOwnerFieldsExceptionHandler}, which responds 400 with an {@code errors}
 * array naming each missing field.
 */
public class MissingOwnerFieldsException extends Exception {

    private final List<String> fields;

    public MissingOwnerFieldsException(List<String> fields) {
        super("Missing required owner fields: " + fields);
        this.fields = List.copyOf(fields);
    }

    public List<String> getFields() {
        return this.fields;
    }
}
```

Result: missing/blank required field → HTTP 400 with body `{"errors": ["firstName", "lastName", ...]}` in the order checked.

There is also a generic `NotFoundException` escalation registered (`.../escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.NotFoundException.yml` → `NotFoundExceptionHandler`), but it is not reachable from the create-owner pipeline (no lookup happens).

