## Enumerated pipeline (validations and side-effects, strict order)

1. Security gate (`composition.authorize`): require `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`, else reject.
2. `ValidateOwnerRequiredFields` (outside transaction): bind body via `@RequestBody` (no `@Valid`); check blank/null in order firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone; if any → throw `MissingOwnerFieldsException` → handler returns 400 `{"errors":[...]}`. Else republish DTO. (DTO `@Pattern`/`@Size`/`@NotNull` NOT enforced.)
3. `BuildOwner` (in transaction): `ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)` — id ignored, pets ignored; no validation.
4. `SaveOwner` (in transaction): `ownerRepository.save(owner)` — point where entity/Person constraints (`@NotEmpty` on firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone, `@Digits`+`@Pattern` 10-digit telephone) can fire if JPA validation is active.
5. `RespondWithOwnerCreated` (in transaction): map to `OwnerDto`, return 201 with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.

No Spring MVC controller shadows this route; the OfficeFloor pipeline is the only path.
